@page "/providers/"
<LibrarianSeoHead Title="Storage providers — Librarian" Description="Compare Librarian Memory, FileSystem, Redis, PostgreSQL, MongoDB, and Cosmos DB providers: persistence, setup, indexes, and query behavior." Path="/providers/" />
<Section Class="shell page-intro"><Span Class="eyebrow">STORAGE PROVIDERS</Span><H1>Choose your<br /><em>storage.</em></H1><Paragraph>Keep a consistent document API.<br />Choose storage based on persistence, sharing, and query needs.</Paragraph></Section>
<Section Class="shell comparison-section"><Div Class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" aria-label="Storage provider comparison"><table><caption>Provider behavior at a glance</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Capability</th><th scope="col">Memory</th><th scope="col">FileSystem</th><th scope="col">Redis</th><th scope="col">PostgreSQL</th><th scope="col">MongoDB</th><th scope="col">Cosmos DB</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Documents live in</th><td>Process memory</td><td>Memory + JSON file</td><td>Redis</td><td>PostgreSQL</td><td>MongoDB</td><td>Cosmos DB</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Persistence</th><td>Temporary</td><td>Periodic save (~5s)</td><td>Write-through¹</td><td>Committed writes</td><td>Committed writes</td><td>Committed writes</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Shared across instances</th><td>No</td><td>No</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Index lifetime</th><td>Until unload</td><td>Rebuilt on reload</td><td>Persisted in Redis</td><td>Persisted in PostgreSQL</td><td>Persisted in MongoDB</td><td>Persisted in Cosmos DB</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Atomic batches</th><td>Yes</td><td>Yes, saved immediately</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes</td><td>Within Cosmos execution limits</td></tr></tbody></table></Div><Paragraph Class="table-note">¹ Redis persistence and eviction configuration determine durability. FileSystem uses one database owner per file; call Save() to flush explicitly.</Paragraph></Section>
<Div Class="shell provider-details">
<Section Id="memory"><Div><Span Class="eyebrow">01 / IN PROCESS</Span><H2 Class="provider-heading"><img class="provider-logo" src="/images/providers/memory.svg" alt="" width="42" height="42" />Memory</H2><Paragraph>For temporary data, tests, and applications that don’t need storage to survive a restart. No external service to configure.</Paragraph><Anchor Href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/Soenneker.Librarian.Memory" Class="text-link">Package on NuGet ↗</Anchor></Div><Div><CodeSample Label="INSTALL" Text="dotnet add package Soenneker.Librarian.Memory" /><CodeSample Label="REGISTER" Text="using Soenneker.Librarian.Memory.Registrars;&#10;&#10;builder.Services.AddMemoryLibrarianDatabaseAsSingleton();" /><Paragraph Class="table-note">Scoped registrations are also available. A scoped memory database owns its own data.</Paragraph></Div></Section>
<Section Id="filesystem"><Div><Span Class="eyebrow">02 / LOCAL JSON</Span><H2 Class="provider-heading"><img class="provider-logo" src="/images/providers/filesystem.svg" alt="" width="42" height="42" />FileSystem</H2><Paragraph>In-memory access with a JSON file behind it. Designed for a single database owner, with periodic saves and immediate persistence for atomic batches.</Paragraph><Paragraph>Await <code>database.Save()</code> for an explicit flush. Dispose the database’s owner asynchronously to complete shutdown persistence.</Paragraph></Div><Div><CodeSample Label="INSTALL & REGISTER" Text="dotnet add package Soenneker.Librarian.FileSystem" /><CodeSample Label="C#" Text="using Soenneker.Librarian.FileSystem.Registrars;&#10;&#10;builder.Services.AddFileSystemLibrarianDatabaseAsSingleton();" /><CodeSample Label="APPSETTINGS.JSON" Text="@FileConfig" /></Div></Section>
<Section Id="redis"><Div><Span Class="eyebrow">03 / SHARED STORAGE</Span><H2 Class="provider-heading"><img class="provider-logo" src="/images/providers/redis.svg" alt="" width="42" height="42" />Redis</H2><Paragraph>Shared documents and persisted indexes for multiple application instances. Reads fetch current Redis data; writes update documents and indexes together.</Paragraph><Paragraph>No RedisJSON, Redis Search, or Lua required. Use a non-evicting database; cluster deployments require Redis 8 or later.</Paragraph><Anchor Href="https://github.com/soenneker/soenneker.librarian.suite/blob/main/docs/REDIS.md" Class="text-link">Redis setup &amp; guarantees ↗</Anchor></Div><Div><CodeSample Label="INSTALL" Text="dotnet add package Soenneker.Librarian.Redis" /><CodeSample Label="C#" Text="using Soenneker.Librarian.Redis.Registrars;&#10;&#10;builder.Services.AddRedisLibrarianDatabaseAsSingleton();" /><CodeSample Label="APPSETTINGS.JSON" Text="@RedisConfig" /></Div></Section>
<Section Id="postgres"><Div><Span Class="eyebrow">04 / PERSISTENT SQL</Span><H2 Class="provider-heading"><img class="provider-logo" src="/images/providers/postgres.svg" alt="" width="42" height="42" />PostgreSQL</H2><Paragraph>Shared persistent documents with SQL-backed filtering, sorting, paging, and aggregates. Writes and conditional batches commit immediately.</Paragraph><Paragraph>Indexes persist across restarts. Requires PostgreSQL 16 or later. Supply connection credentials through your application’s secret configuration.</Paragraph><Anchor Href="https://github.com/soenneker/soenneker.librarian.suite/blob/main/docs/POSTGRES.md" Class="text-link">PostgreSQL setup &amp; queries ↗</Anchor></Div><Div><CodeSample Label="INSTALL" Text="dotnet add package Soenneker.Librarian.Postgres" /><CodeSample Label="C#" Text="using Soenneker.Librarian.Postgres.Registrars;&#10;&#10;builder.Services.AddPostgresLibrarianDatabaseAsSingleton();" /><Paragraph>Configure <code>Librarian:Postgres:ConnectionString</code> and <code>Librarian:Postgres:Key</code>.</Paragraph></Div></Section>
<Section Id="mongo"><Div><Span Class="eyebrow">05 / NATIVE DOCUMENTS</Span><H2 Class="provider-heading"><img class="provider-logo" src="/images/providers/mongo.svg" alt="" width="42" height="42" />MongoDB</H2><Paragraph>Stores Document fields directly in native collections, with immediate writes, server-side LINQ, versioned writes, and atomic conditional batches across collections. MongoDB creates its _id index automatically. Configure secondary indexes explicitly with EnsureIndex or MongoDB tooling; reads do not create indexes.</Paragraph><Paragraph>Atomic batches require a MongoDB replica set or sharded cluster with transaction support. Configure <code>Librarian:Mongo:ConnectionString</code>, <code>DatabaseName</code>, and <code>Key</code>. Optional <code>CollectionName</code> defaults to <code>librarian</code>.</Paragraph></Div><Div><CodeSample Label="INSTALL" Text="dotnet add package Soenneker.Librarian.Mongo" /><CodeSample Label="C#" Text="using Soenneker.Librarian.Mongo.Registrars;&#10;&#10;builder.Services.AddMongoLibrarianDatabaseAsSingleton();" /></Div></Section>
<Section Id="cosmos"><Div><Span Class="eyebrow">06 / AZURE DOCUMENTS</Span><H2 Class="provider-heading"><img class="provider-logo" src="/images/providers/cosmos.svg" alt="" width="42" height="42" />Cosmos DB for NoSQL</H2><Paragraph>Creates the database and physical container on first access. Documents use native Cosmos point operations, automatic JSON indexing, and SDK LINQ queries. Librarian does not change indexing policies; multi-field ordering requires a composite index configured in Cosmos.</Paragraph><Paragraph>Documents use their own <code>DocumentId</code> and <code>PartitionKey</code>; each logical container has a physical Cosmos container. Explicit partition-scoped containers, cross-partition queries, native continuation paging, and versioned conditional writes are also supported. Conditional batches stay within one physical container and one partition and use the native TransactionalBatch API with ETag checks or create-only writes. Batches allow at most 100 writes; Cosmos request size and partition limits apply.</Paragraph></Div><Div><CodeSample Label="INSTALL" Text="dotnet add package Soenneker.Librarian.Cosmos" /><CodeSample Label="C#" Text="using Soenneker.Librarian.Cosmos.Registrars;&#10;&#10;builder.Services.AddCosmosLibrarianDatabaseAsSingleton();" /><Paragraph>Uses <code>Azure:Cosmos:Endpoint</code>, <code>AccountKey</code>, <code>DatabaseName</code>, <code>DatabaseThroughput</code>, <code>DatabaseThroughputType</code>, and the application's <code>Environment</code>. Optional <code>Librarian:Cosmos:ContainerName</code> and <code>Key</code> both default to <code>librarian</code>.</Paragraph><Paragraph>Database and container creation are enabled by default. The <code>EnsureDatabaseOnFirstUse</code> and <code>EnsureContainerOnFirstUse</code> settings remain available for pre-provisioned environments.</Paragraph></Div></Section>
<Section Id="couchdb"><Div><Span Class="eyebrow">07 / HTTP DOCUMENTS</Span><H2 Class="provider-heading"><img class="provider-logo" src="/images/providers/couchdb.svg" alt="" width="42" height="42" />CouchDB</H2><Paragraph>Creates a physical CouchDB database for each logical container on first access. Stores Document JSON directly, with revision-checked writes, partition-scoped handles, and explicit Mango indexes. Unloading releases local handles and preserves remote data.</Paragraph><Paragraph>Call EnsureIndex before indexed queries. CouchDB native collation applies. LINQ and atomic multi-document batches are unsupported; use JSON-path query methods and single-document revision checks.</Paragraph></Div><Div><CodeSample Label="PROJECT" Text="Soenneker.Librarian.CouchDb" /><CodeSample Label="C#" Text="using Soenneker.Librarian.CouchDb.Registrars;&#10;&#10;builder.Services.AddCouchDbLibrarianDatabaseAsSingleton();" /><Paragraph>Configure <code>Librarian:CouchDb:Endpoint</code>, optional <code>Username</code> and <code>Password</code>, and <code>Key</code>. <code>DatabasePrefix</code> and <code>Key</code> default to <code>librarian</code>. <code>EnsureDatabaseOnFirstUse</code> defaults to true; disable it for pre-provisioned databases. Requires CouchDB 3.5 or later.</Paragraph></Div></Section>
</Div>
<Section Class="shell provider-ending"><H2>Same API. Know the differences.</H2><Paragraph>Memory and FileSystem can fall back to local evaluation for unsupported queries. Redis and PostgreSQL reject unsupported expressions. MongoDB and Cosmos delegate LINQ translation to their native SDKs, including supported grouping, aggregates, and projections. Their native query semantics and translation limits apply; unsupported expressions are rejected without client-side fallback. Review query support before moving a workload between providers.</Paragraph><Anchor Href="https://github.com/soenneker/soenneker.librarian.suite/blob/main/docs/QUERY-CAPABILITIES.md" Class="button">Compare query capabilities ↗</Anchor></Section>
@code {
    private const string FileConfig = """
        {
          "Librarian": {
            "FileSystem": { "FilePath": "data/librarian.json" }
          }
        }
        """;
    private const string RedisConfig = """
        {
          "Azure": { "Redis": { "ConnectionString": "localhost:6379" } },
          "Librarian": {
            "Redis": { "Key": "my-app:librarian" }
          }
        }
        """;
}
